<SiteLayout title="About HaloForge Labs | Halowin Bubo" description="HaloForge Labs builds Halowin Bubo, an open-source local LLM server that runs Qwen3.8 Flash Next on AMD Strix Halo (Ryzen AI Max+ 395) under Windows.">
  <span class="eyebrow">HaloForge Labs</span>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="intro">HaloForge Labs builds Halowin Bubo, a local LLM server for AMD Strix Halo on Windows. <a href="/bubo/">Read about Halowin Bubo</a> or <a href="/docs/">open the documentation</a>.</p>
  <div class="article-grid">
    <section class="article-body"><h2>Built on gufo</h2><p>Bubo is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/gufo-org/gufo">gufo</a>, the open-source LLM server. The gufo authors wrote the upstream server and release it under the MIT license. The Windows port comes from pixmaate’s gufo fork.</p><h2>The name</h2><p>Halowin joins Halo, from Strix Halo, and Windows. Bubo is a genus of owls. Gufo is the Italian word for owl.</p><p>The owl in our logo is the Egyptian hieroglyph for owl (G17), drawn from the Noto Sans Egyptian Hieroglyphs font under the SIL Open Font License. The text of this site is set in ET Book, by Dmitry Krasny, Bonnie Scranton and Edward Tufte, under the MIT license. The review layer on this site, shown only to reviewers, is <a href="https://github.com/reviewjs/annotate">annotate.js</a>, under the MIT license; the license text is in <a href="/vendor/annotate-LICENSE.txt">annotate-LICENSE.txt</a>.</p></section>
    <aside class="margin-note"><span class="eyebrow">Source and support</span><p><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo">Source code</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/issues">Report an issue</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/releases">Releases</a></p></aside>
  </div>
